### Exhaustive retained-source dependency audit

These are **all** retained `mod`/`use` edges to excluded modules, using original reference line numbers:

| Reference location | Exact line to remove | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `src/lib.rs:19` | `pub mod ffi;` | C ABI/ctypes surface is rebuilt in Task 1.4, C5 |
| `src/lib.rs:21` | `pub mod joint_matching;` | C2 candidate-matching policy machinery |
| `src/lib.rs:22` | `pub mod myolie_features;` | C4 flat v2 observation encoder; Task 1.3 rebuild |
| `src/lib.rs:23` | `pub mod myolie_sampler;` | C3 grammar is a reviewed port in Task 1.2 |
| `src/lib.rs:24` | `pub mod native_agents;` | C2 scripted opponents; selected imports belong to Phase 7 |
| `src/lib.rs:25` | `pub mod policy_rows;` | C2 policy action-row machinery |
| `src/lib.rs:27` | `pub mod training;` | C5 collector/lifecycle is rebuilt, not vendored |

Remove each whole line including its LF; retain blank lines and all other bytes. Expected resulting `lib.rs`: **185,626 bytes**, SHA-256 **`c4b9bac5057be3a435d2f1035aae17bcd15e7f95ea8557322e4929877c8231fd`**. This hash was calculated by applying the seven removals in memory, not by installing or compiling a trimmed crate.

There are **no other excluded-module imports** in the retained implementation or RNG test. `lib.rs` retains `mod econ_attrib`, its `pub use econ_attrib::{ATTRIB_FIELDS, ATTRIB_VERBS, ATTRIB_VERSION}`, `pub mod py_random`, and `use py_random::PyRandom`. `econ_attrib.rs:10` uses `super::*`, resolving to the retained library; `lib.rs` unit tests use `super::*` and `crate::econ_attrib::*`, also retained. `py_random.rs` and its integration test depend only on the retained generator and numeric crates. Bins/examples are not dependencies of these files. No `rayon` use survives in the three sources or RNG test.

No extra public wrapper is necessary. Reference APIs already provide:

```rust
Game::new(config: Config, seed: i64, num_agents: usize) -> Result<Game, String>
Game::new_with_seed_decimal(config: Config, seed: &str, num_agents: usize) -> Result<Game, String>
Game::step(&mut self, actions: &[serde_json::Value]) -> Result<(), String>
Game::step_with_market_metrics(&mut self, actions: &[serde_json::Value]) -> Result<StepMetrics, String>
Game::public_state(&self) -> PublicState
Game::snapshot(&self) -> StepSnapshot
Game::terminal_banks(&self) -> Option<&[f64]>
Game::econ_counters(&self) -> Option<&[[u64; ECON_FIELDS]; 2]>
Game::attrib_counters(&self) -> Option<&[[u64; ATTRIB_FIELDS]; 2]>
```

The seed/config constructor starts at step 0. `step` consumes already decoded per-seat JSON command objects (`farmer`, `hands`, `market`), not policy slots; new grammar decoding is outside Task 1.1. State includes both privates for native adapters; this is not permission to expose the rival's private state to a model. `ECON_FIELDS=32`, `ATTRIB_FIELDS=167`; counters remain telemetry, not observation history.

